<BaseLayout title="About" description="The purpose and point of view behind Built to Change, a technical blog about building software that evolves.">
  <header class="page-intro wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
    <h1>Software is built twice: in thought, then in code.</h1>
    <p>Built to Change is a place to make the thinking behind technical work visible.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="about-layout wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The name points to a practical question: when the next requirement arrives, how much of the system
        will need to move? Architecture, engineering habits, programming choices, and AI tools all shape that
        answer.
      </p>
      <h2>What belongs here</h2>
      <p>
        This notebook explores software architecture, the day-to-day craft of engineering, the decisions made
        while programming, and ways to use AI while keeping human judgment in the loop. The aim is to explain
        ideas through their trade-offs and show where they are useful, where they are not, and what questions
        they leave open.
      </p>
      <p>
        Expect essays and working notes rather than universal recipes. A pattern that helps one team can
        burden another; context is part of the design. The most useful outcome is a clearer way to reason
        about the next change.
      </p>
      <h2>Start with a question</h2>
      <p>
        Browse the <a href="/writing/">writing archive</a>, subscribe with <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>, or
        visit the <a href="https://github.com/thiagoamaroalves" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub profile</a>
        behind this site.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="profile-card">
      <div class="profile-symbol" aria-hidden="true">&lt;/&gt;</div>
      <h2><a href="https://github.com/thiagoamaroalves" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">@thiagoamaroalves</a></h2>
      <p>Writing about ideas and trade-offs for building software that evolves.</p>
      <p>Architecture · Engineering · Programming · AI</p>
      <a href="https://github.com/thiagoamaroalves" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Find me on GitHub ↗</a>
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
